SCOPE — what this licence does and does not cover

This licence covers only the contribution made in this repository: the code, the
derived quantities computed by it (air kerma rate constants, spectrum-solved half-
and tenth-value layers, per-line dose shares), and the accompanying documentation.

It does NOT and cannot license the evaluated data this work is built on. Those
remain the work of the bodies below and are used under their own terms:

  Decay data — IAEA Nuclear Data Section, Livechart of Nuclides (ENSDF),
  International Atomic Energy Agency, Vienna.
  <https://nds.iaea.org/relnsd/vcharthtml/VChartHTML.html>
  Used with acknowledgement under the IAEA website terms of use, which permit
  reproduction and dissemination of IAEA data provided the IAEA is credited as
  the source. The IAEA does not endorse this work, its methods or its results.

  Photon interaction coefficients — J. H. Hubbell and S. M. Seltzer, Tables of
  X-Ray Mass Attenuation Coefficients and Mass Energy-Absorption Coefficients
  from 1 keV to 20 MeV for Elements Z = 1 to 92 and 48 Additional Substances of
  Dosimetric Interest, NISTIR 5632, NIST Standard Reference Database 126,
  National Institute of Standards and Technology. <https://doi.org/10.18434/T4D01F>
  NIST Standard Reference Database 126, (c) 1989, 1990, 1996 by the U.S. Secretary
  of Commerce on behalf of the United States of America, all rights reserved.
  These tables are used here for computation and are not redistributed. NIST does
  not endorse this work and makes no warranty as to the accuracy of any result
  derived from these data.

This software does not replace a shielding design, a dose assessment or a
radiation survey by a qualified person.
